    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><dateline><date when="1948-06-28">June 28, 1948</date></dateline><salute>My
                        dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Mr.
                        Tillich</rs>:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>We are preparing a new and completely revised edition of the Funk &amp; Wagnalls
                    New Standard Encyclopedia. This new work will have a Consulting and Advisory
                    Board whose members will read and criticize a small number of articles that fall
                    in their particular fields. Their comments will then be sent on to us so that we
                    may make whatever changes are necessary.</p>
                <p>I am writing you to ask if you would care to join our Board.</p>
                <p>Our fee for articles up to 1000 words is $ 10.; longer articles are remunerated
                    at $ 15. each.</p>
                <p>Would you please let me know at your earliest convenience whather we can count on
                    your assistance.</p>
                <closer><salute>Very truly yours,</salute><signed><hi rend="hand"><rs
                                ref="#tillich_place_id__5152" type="person">Harold
                            Friedlander</rs></hi><lb/><rs ref="#tillich_place_id__5152"
                            type="person">Harold Friedlander</rs><lb/>Managing Editor<note type="ea"
                            >Am oberen Blattrand steht maschinenschriftlich: <q>Have answered that
                                he will receive a delayed reply from you</q>.</note></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
